<section aria-labelledby="homelife-engagement-title">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="section-label">The campaign brief</div>
    <h2 id="homelife-engagement-title">Give past real estate leads something timely to talk about.</h2>
    <p class="cs2-intro">HomeLife had older residential and commercial leads. We called to reconnect and see whether their property plans were still active. The campaign also promoted a webinar on property values, home prices, and where the real estate market might go next. The webinar included discussion of Western Canada and the Greater Toronto Area (GTA). <a href="https://www.homelife.ca/">About HomeLife Realty <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="homelife-campaign-title">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="section-label">Two ways to reengage</div>
    <h2 id="homelife-campaign-title">The event invitation and the appointment served different needs.</h2>
    <p class="cs2-intro">The webinar gave people a way to hear about home prices and property values even if they were early in their decision. A follow-up appointment gave someone with a specific question time to talk through it with HomeLife.</p>
    <div class="cs2-signal-grid">
      <article><span>Webinar outreach</span><h3>Offer a market update</h3><p>We explained what the webinar would cover and invited prospects to register. A registration showed that someone wanted to hear the broader market discussion.</p></article>
      <article><span>Lead follow-up</span><h3>Set up a one-to-one conversation</h3><p>We arranged appointments for prospects who wanted a direct follow-up. Each booking gave HomeLife a time to discuss that person’s real estate needs.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
